-- title:
--   Mod p eigensystem on Γ_H(N) occurs in weight two for Γ₀(N)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be an odd prime, $N$ a positive integer, $H$ a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times$, $S_0$ a set of natural numbers, $S$ a finite set of natural numbers and $n \colon \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{Z}$. Let $\Gamma_H(N) \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ be the image of the preimage of $H$ under the lower-right-entry character $\Gamma_0(N) \to (\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times$, and let $\varphi_0$ be an additive homomorphism from $\Gamma_H(N)$, written additively, to $\mathbb{Z}$; assume $\varphi_0$ lies in the submodule [`ModularCurve.Period.parabolicHoms`](def/ModularCurve_PeriodMap.html#L62) of parabolic homomorphisms, that $\varphi_0$ is not of the form $p\psi$, that for every $\sigma \in \Gamma_0(N)$ the class $\varphi_0 \circ \mathrm{conj}_\sigma - \varphi_0$ (the raw diamond operator minus the identity) is $p$ times such a homomorphism, and that for every prime $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid N$ one has $T_\ell \varphi_0 - n(\ell)\varphi_0 \in p \cdot H^1$, where $T_\ell$ is [`CohCarrier.heckeT`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L250), the transfer from $\Gamma_H^{\mathrm{up}}(N,\ell)$ composed with the conjugation map `conjL`. Let $k$ be a field of characteristic $p$ and $\bar\rho$ a [`ResidualGaloisRep`](def/GaloisRep_Residual.html#L22) over $k$: a two-dimensional $k$-space $V$ with a multiplicative map $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}) \to \mathrm{End}_k V$ factoring through a finite level; assume $\bar\rho$ is absolutely irreducible, i.e. its base change to $\overline{k}$ is irreducible. If $p = 3$, assume in addition that for every field $K$ over $k$ and every index-two subgroup $G$ of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$, each $K$-submodule of $K \otimes_k V$ stable under all of $G$ is $\bot$ or $\top$. Finally assume that for every prime $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid N$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $A$, and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ acting as the $\ell$-power map on the residue field, $\mathrm{tr}\,\bar\rho(\sigma)$ equals the image of $n(\ell)$ in $k$. Then the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S₀`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for $\ell \notin S_0$ — has a maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}$ containing $p$ such that $T_\ell - n(\ell) \in \mathfrak{m}$ for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S_0$ and $\ell \notin S$.
--
--   This is the character-switching step in weight two, after Carayol: a mod $p$ system of Hecke eigenvalues realised by a parabolic integral class on $\Gamma_H(N)$ which is diamond-invariant modulo $p$, and whose residual representation is absolutely irreducible, is already realised on $\Gamma_0(N)$. It is used in the passage from the Frey curve's residual representation to a normalised eigenform of the expected level, feeding the level-lowering arguments that produce eigenforms of level dividing $N$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CohCarrier_exists_isMaximal_heckeAlgebra_mem_of_mem_parabolicHoms_of_isAbsolutelyIrreducible.lean

